@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-shared-handoff-requires-verified-foreground-source
The app MUST activate and consume native handoff storage only for its actual verified
eligible foreground source, using the existing shared source namespace. A source or
scene replacement during native reading MUST prevent delivery. Sign-in or confirmed
anonymous state MUST revoke the native handoff audience; checking, network problems,
same-account renewal and scene close MUST preserve durable same-source pending data.
Cross-framework handoff MUST use the bounded canonical payload string, decoded again
in PullyShared before the existing inbox receives its typed destination. Source:
the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native share handoff and account-isolation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-share-import-retains-its-verified-foreground-grant
Native import MUST wait for the current AccountObservationOwner's verified foreground
grant. A pause and resume during native reading MUST reject the old delivery even
when the same account/source returns. Scene close MUST preserve durable pending data;
explicit entry into Explore MUST revoke private handoff authority before publishing
that mode. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 source-owned native share plan and Tavi's
22 Oct 2026 shared Guest/private workspace and lifecycle isolation requirements.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-personal-store-is-one-opaque-native-vault
The native personal-account store MUST adapt the same shared PersonalSessionVault
through a throwing Cocoa storage port, without requiring Swift to construct an
unexported client model. One application-wide vault and UI-dispatcher cleanup
lifetime MUST be shared across scenes. Secure-store failure MUST remain a fixed
retryable failure rather than an empty successful read or write. A missing record
MUST remain distinct from a thrown read and from an existing empty or corrupt blob
across the Cocoa boundary. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 personal-account request and
the accepted 22 Oct native bridge plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-personal-identity-retires-all-public-scenes
Personal promotion or sign-out MUST synchronously revoke every older public runtime
before any scene observer runs. A late response or retained sign-in callback from
an older identity MUST NOT publish a profile or dispatch a new attempt. Observer
cleanup failure in one scene MUST NOT keep another old runtime current. The origin
MUST come only from explicit trusted application configuration and MUST NOT inherit
the saved legacy server or grant private authority. Missing configuration MUST keep
personal work unavailable without preventing Explore. Source: Tavi's public-read
personal-account decision and the accepted 22 Oct one-vault/multiple-scene plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-personal-foreground-has-an-explicit-native-port
The mounted personal flow MUST receive synchronous active/inactive events from the
actual scene, independent of Compose frames and Home's started/background events.
A host without that real adapter MUST leave personal sign-in unavailable. Ordinary
inactivity MUST retain the same sign-in owner and MUST NOT cancel an already accepted
bounded claim. Source: the independent 22 Oct mounted lifecycle finding and accepted
native activity-adapter plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] ios-personal-mount-keeps-public-authority
Only the public workspace MAY open the native personal runtime and shared account
sheet. Its verified profile MUST remain on tokenless public Explore; personal
connection MUST NOT construct legacy account, Home, AI, Stats or settings observers
or attach its bearer to public GitHub reads. Entry renewal MUST retire the old
runtime, sheet, palette and native callbacks before the replacement public workspace
mounts. Private selection and strict Debug fixture constructors MUST retain their
existing owners without adopting personal credentials. Source: Tavi's personal
GitHub/public-browsing request and accepted 22 Oct native public-account mount plan.
